  "source": "The Swedish Council for Information on Alcohol and Other Drugs (CAN)",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of pupils in school year 9 and pupils below the age of 18 in year 2 of upper secondary school that smoke, use snus or vape and state that they normally purchase tobacco and nicotine products themselves. Question: 'How do you normally get hold of tobacco and nicotine products?' The indicator refers to the percentage that chose the options 'Buys personally in a physical store', 'buys personally in an online store', 'buys personally via social media contact' or 'buys personally from a dealer (without social media contact)."
  ]
